WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
When a Claude Code session ends,

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.860
the conversation is gone,

3
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.660
but the next one starts with the project's instructions.

4
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.220
That's because Claude Code memory lives in files on disk,

5
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.780
not in the conversation.

6
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.160
The first is CLAUDE.md,

7
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:14.860
which you write,

8
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.860
and it's read only at startup,

9
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.833
so a mid-session edit waits for the next session.

10
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:21.433
The second is auto memory,

11
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.773
which Claude Code writes as it works,

12
00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:27.167
with MEMORY.md indexing its topic files.

13
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.607
An outdated note is worse than none,

14
00:00:29.607 --> 00:00:33.233
because the agent trusts it and writes code that breaks.

15
00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:37.333
So I'd run /memory to see what's loaded and remove stale instructions.
